# YouTube on VPS/datacenter IPs (Contabo, AWS, etc.) requires cookies.txt.
#
# === STEP-BY-STEP (Firefox — required, Chrome cookies often fail) ===
#
# 1. Install Firefox and log in to https://www.youtube.com
# 2. Install extension: "Get cookies.txt LOCALLY"
#    https://addons.mozilla.org/firefox/addon/cookies-txt/
# 3. On youtube.com, click the extension → Export → "Current site"
# 4. Save the file as cookies.txt
# 5. Verify the file contains lines with ".youtube.com" in them
#
# === Coolify deployment ===
#
# 1. In your backend app → Persistent Storage → add a file mount:
#      Container path: /app/cookies.txt
#      Upload your cookies.txt file
# 2. OR set env: COOKIES_FILE=/app/cookies.txt
# 3. Rebuild & redeploy the backend (not just restart)
#
# === Optional: PO Token sidecar (if cookies alone fail) ===
#
# Deploy a second Coolify service:
#   Image: brainicism/bgutil-ytdlp-pot-provider:latest
#   Port: 4416 (internal only)
# Then set backend env:
#   BGUTIL_POT_BASE_URL=http://<bgutil-service-hostname>:4416
#
# Cookies expire — re-export every few weeks if downloads stop working.
